      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f2f725cfbd1a1558bf3945d|full_name}: If you are being targeted by username in such a way, report the world. Worlds have a rather limited space in which they are allowed to apply per-user moderations, and this would clearly not be one of them. Plus, this would be relatively harmless. It is really really easy for a world to entirely crash you with no error message or log whatsoever if they wanted to, and that has been the case for several years now, mainly because of Unity being Unity. The reason why this won't happen is because World Creators are not evil people and they spend a lot of time creating an experience that you enjoy, while people who disrupts that experience are usually other users who have nothing to loose because they don't rely on their account and can just create another one. World creators on the other side don't want their world or account being removed, so they won't target you like that even if they hate you, because it's not worth the risk.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
